src/vendor/datasketches/ is the files listed in
tools/vendor/keep/datasketches.txt, copied with their upstream layout from the
Apache source release, with exactly the patches above applied: LICENSE, NOTICE
and every component's include/
directory. The library is header-only, so nothing else is needed; src/Makevars
puts each include/ directory on the include path. Tests, benchmarks, Python
bindings and the CMake build are excluded. tools/vendor/manifest.tsv pins the
archive and its sha256; tools/vendor/verify re-derives the tree from it and
fails on any other difference.

Both patches close deserialization bugs that remain in 5.3.1, found by
tools/fuzz (data.sketches issue #33), and are to be reported upstream:

0001-hll-validate-lg-k.patch rejects an HLL image whose lg_k lies outside
[MIN_LOG_K, MAX_LOG_K]. The array, coupon-list and coupon-set deserializers
used it unchecked as a shift count (undefined behavior for lg_k > 32).

0002-bloom-require-standard-preamble.patch rejects a non-empty Bloom filter
image with the empty-filter preamble, which made the parser read the bit
count past the bytes it had checked (heap over-read).

Updating: change the tag, commit, version_string, archive and archive_sha256
columns of tools/vendor/manifest.tsv (check the archive against the .sha512
Apache publishes beside it), regenerate the keep list from the new release's
include/ directories if components gained or lost files, and run
tools/vendor/fetch. Then update this file, R/datasketches-version.R,
inst/COPYRIGHTS and DESCRIPTION's Authors@R against the new NOTICE and
LICENSE, and run tools/vendor/verify and the test suite.
